<urn:atm:triage:finding/QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "QA-002" ;
  triage:title "#[allow(dead_code)] should be #[expect(dead_code)] per M-LINT-OVERRIDE-EXPECT" ;
  triage:description "AG23-QA-1 (rust-qa-agent, minor): one or more #[allow(dead_code)] annotations introduced/retained by the AG.23 diff should use #[expect(dead_code)] instead, per the repo's M-LINT-OVERRIDE-EXPECT lint-override convention (expect fails loudly once the code is no longer dead; allow silently permits it forever)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "lint-convention" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "absent" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T12:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:notes "Sweep pattern '#\\[allow\\(dead_code\\)\\]' (exact match) found no occurrences in any AG sprint worktree (AG.18-AG.25) or integrate/phase-AG. All #[allow(dead_code)] annotations in the codebase use the reason= parameter format: #[allow(dead_code, reason=\"...\")]. No violations of the exact pattern exist. Separate RBQA-F004 triage addresses the cfg_attr(not(test), allow(dead_code)) test-only violations." .

